            <ArticleTitle>Mirtazapine associated with recurrent pancreatitis - a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>336-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/0269881107081517</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pancreatitis can be a rare but serious side-effect of Mirtazapine. There are very few case reports worldwide that highlight this. We present a case of recurrent pancreatitis which demonstrates this potential clinical association.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
